    "created_at": "2020-08-25T02:11:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-25T02:11:42Z",
    "body": "Also, it isn't such a big change, as the [RDFa in XHTML: Syntax and Processing](https://www.w3.org/TR/rdfa-syntax/#sec_6.3.1.1.) already allows the ```@property``` on the meta tag, but only in the ```<head>```. Example in the spec:\r\n\r\n> ```html\r\n> <meta about=\"http://internet-apps.blogspot.com/\"\r\n>      property=\"dc:creator\" content=\"Mark Birbeck\" />\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThus, what I'm proposing is a rather small change:\r\n\r\n 1. Allow ```<meta>``` tags with RDFa attributes within ```<body>```. (already allowed within ```<head>```)\r\n 2. Allow mixing RDFa and Microdata attributes in ```<meta>``` tags.\r\n\r\nWhile these changes might give some work to plugins and semantic web tools, I don't see how it impact browsers as they don't have to change their behavior.",
